	"_readme": [
		"Rules for tools/food_diversity.py (plan_food_diversity_1121.md section 3). The tool writes every food's diversity",
		"into solRaspberryPie's diversity.json (values + families); a jar rebuild applies it.",
		"q = hunger x (1 + saturation modifier) / 2. curve: [q, value] anchors, linear between, flat past the last.",
		"topRank: the multiplier lifts the tier's (topRank+1)-th best food to the top, so one outlier does not set it; above it values cap.",
		"tierTops: best food of each tier (R2). Tiers low / mid / high are by q (lowMax, midMax) or Nourishment = high;",
		"their values are capped at the top. dragon, gilded, feast, golden get a multiplier fitted to the top.",
		"ceilings: after all rules, each tier is scaled so the cumulative columns (none, no dragon, ... low only) peak at the listed targets, one per chain step (plan R15; without targets, evenly spaced from top to low, R14); tierTops are the values before this scale.",
		"canShare: a can scores this share of its source (R4). nonFood: value of a non-food recipe input (R9);",
		"containers score 0. families: members share one diet entry and one value (R5, R6)."
